{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Behold now, I know that you are a woman of beautiful appearance.</b> The language of <b>הנה</b> is the presentation of a thing, as in (Genesis 19:20) ״הנה נא העיר הזאת קרובה״, ״הנה האש והעצים״, (Genesis 22:7) ״ויאמר הנני״. And the word נא is language of entreaty. And Scripture says:" "<b>By way of the plain sense (peshat):</b> I am prepared to entreat you, and what is the entreaty? — <b>I know that you are a woman of beautiful appearance</b>, and it shall come to pass when the Egyptians see you, etc., Say now, you are my sister — and everything is drawn toward the verse 'Say now (אמרי נא).'" "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> 'Behold now, I know that you are a woman of beautiful appearance' — Abraham said to her: the exertion of the journey diminishes beauty and removes the radiance of the face, yet you stand in your beauty — behold now, I know that you are a woman of beautiful appearance. And the opinion of our Rabbis of blessed memory is that he had never gazed upon her until that hour, for Abraham, because of his great modesty, would make a covenant with his eyes, in the manner of what Job said (Job 31:1) ״ברית כרתי לעיני״, for the righteous make a covenant with their limbs not to harm them, like a person who makes a covenant with his enemies not to harm him, as it is said (Exodus 23:32) ״לא תכרות להם ולאלהיהם ברית״, for you have no enemy that will do a person harm like the harm caused by his own limbs. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: dirt in the mouth of Job, who said ״ומה אתבונן על בתולה״ — 'and why should I gaze upon a virgin?' — meaning: upon others he does not gaze, but upon his own wife he does gaze; but Abraham — even upon his own he did not gaze, as it says, 'Behold now, I know that you are a woman of beautiful appearance.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:07.897421941Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}